C - VARIABLES
==============

Store data in your program.


DECLARING VARIABLES
--------------------
int x;              Create integer
float price;        Create decimal
char letter;        Create character
int numbers[10];    Array of 10 integers


ASSIGN VALUES
-------------
int age = 25;
float height = 5.8;
char grade = 'A';
int arr[3] = {1, 2, 3};


DATA TYPES
----------
int             Whole numbers (-2,000,000,000 to 2,000,000,000)
float           Decimals (less precision)
double          Decimals (more precision)
char            Single character
long            Bigger integers
short           Smaller integers


NAMING RULES
------------
Must start with letter or underscore
Can contain letters, numbers, underscores
No spaces or special characters
Case sensitive: age ≠ AGE


GOOD NAMES
----------
✓ player_name
✓ total_score
✓ isValid
✗ x
✗ data
✗ a1b2c3


SCOPE
-----
Variables inside { } only exist there:

int main() {
    int x = 5;
    // x exists here
}
// x doesn't exist here


TIPS
----
Name variables clearly.
Declare close to usage.
Initialize before using.
